; Sprites: small flyer, left and right (8 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $BC00+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. A small creature in side view, mostly 8 pixels high, that looks like a
; bird or insect with changing wing positions. Frames 0-3 are used while moving left, 4-7 while moving right (bit 7 of
; entity byte +0). Used by entity definitions $0D $14 $15 $16 $17 $18 $19 $1C $25 $5F $68 $6D in rooms $01 $04 $08 $0B
; $0C $0D $0E $0F $10 $14 $16 $24 $26 $2D $30 $32 $36 $38: the most used page.
@label=SpritesSmallFlyers
b$BC00 DEFB $00,$00 ; frame 0: small flyer facing left, frame 0
